    "summary": "Free and open source cross-platform software platform developed by Microsoft For the earlier framework, see .NET Framework . For the top-level domain, see .net . For other uses, see .net (disambiguation) . .NET Developers .NET Foundation and the open-source community Release June 27, 2016 ; 10 years ago ( 2016-06-27 ) Stable release 10.0.12 / 8 September 2026 ; 10 days ago ( 8 September 2026 ) Preview release 10.0.0-rc.2 / 14 October 2025 ; 11 months ago ( 14 October 2025 ) Written in C# , C++ and C Operating system Cross-platform : Windows , Linux , macOS , Android , iOS Platform IA-32 , x86-64 , 64-bit ARM , Power ISA (ppc64le), IBM Z and LinuxONE ( s390x ) Predecessor .NET Framework Type Software framework License MIT Website dotnet .microsoft .com Repository github .com /dotnet /runtime The .NET platform (pronounced as \" dot net\" ; formerly named .NET Core ) is a free and open-source , managed computer software framework for Windows , Linux , and macOS operating systems . It is a cross-platform successor to the .NET Framework . The project is mainly developed by Microsoft employees by way of the .NET Foundation and is today released under an MIT License . New versions of the .NET platform are released annually, typically in November. The most recent version of .NET is .NET 10, released in November 2025, which is a long-term support (LTS) version, and is scheduled to receive updates until November 2028. ^ https://dotnet.microsoft.com/en-us/download/dotnet/10.0 . Retrieved September 9, 2026 . {{ cite web }} : Missing or empty |title= ( help ) ^ \"Download .NET 10.0\" . Retrieved October 14, 2025 . ^ \"Chapter 4. Supported operating systems and architectures | Release Notes for .NET 8.0 RPM packages | .NET | 8.0 | Red Hat Documentation\" . docs.redhat.com . Retrieved September 13, 2025 . ^ a b \"core/LICENSE.TXT\" . GitHub . Archived from the original on July 16, 2021 . Retrieved June 4, 2018 . ^ \"Download .NET Core\" . microsoft.com . Microsoft . Archived from the original on September 3, 2017 . Retrieved October 31, 2017 . ^ Cite error: The named reference :6 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ).",
